  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mukesh Rathaur S/O Shivram Rathaur vs The Senior Police Inspector And Anr on 28 July, 2025 2025:Bhc-As:31745 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Digitally signed Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction by Husenbasha Husenbasha Rahaman Rahaman Nadaf Nadaf Date: 2025.07.29 15:14:34 +0530 Anticipatory Bail Application No.2984 Of 2023 Mukesh Rathaur s/o Shivram Rathaur ... Ap Versus The Sr. Police Inspector and Anr. ... Re **** Mr. Mateen Shaikh a/w. Mr. Rafique Shaikh, for Applicant Ms. R. S. Tenduklar, App for State. Api Vishal Patil, Ndps Cell Nashik City, present. *** * Coram : M.M. Sath Date : 2 P.C. : 1. 2. This is an application for pre-arrest bail in connection with CR No.592 of 2022 registered with Ambad Police Station, Nashik for the offenses under Section 328, 188, 272 & 273 of Indian Penal Code, 1860 ('IPC', for short) and Sections 26(2)(i), 27, 30(2)(a), 26(2)(iv), 3(1)(zz)(iv), 27(3)(e) and 59 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.",
    "facts": "2. This is an application for pre-arrest bail in connection with CR No.592 of 2022 registered with Ambad Police Station, Nashik for the offenses under Section 328, 188, 272 & 273 of Indian Penal Code, 1860 ('IPC', for short) and Sections 26(2)(i), 27, 30(2)(a), 26(2)(iv), 3(1)(zz)(iv), 27(3)(e) and 59 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 3. Admittedly the Applicant is protected by this Court's order dated 26.10.2023, for last about 2 years wherein it is already recorded that the Applicant was named by co-accused who was found in Mukesh Rathaur S/O Shivram Rathaur vs The Senior Police Inspector And Anr on 28 July, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/100568467/ 1 possession of contraband articles being Gutakha Pan Masala. 4. Learned counsel for the Applicant submits that his name was 57 ABA-2984-2023.doc involved only because of vehicle/truck carrying contraband article was earlier owned by the Applicant. It is contended that the Applicant had sold it prior to the date of FIR. 5. Learned APP for the Respondent/State on instructions of Investigating Officer (who is present in the Court), submits that investigation is complete and charge-sheet is already filed and the Applicant is not shown as co-accused.",
